{
  "description": "#6054 D3 — the end conditions `remaining_repeat_bounds` reads on the edge into DONE, and what `copy_repeat_bounds` carries onto the next occurrence. `repeat-until` stops the chain once the shifted due date passes it, and is copied when it does not; with no date to shift it is not checked at all. `repeat-count` stops the chain once `repeat-seq` reaches it, and is copied with `repeat-seq` one higher (from 0 when unset); a `repeat-seq` without a `repeat-count` is not carried. A `++` rule that cannot catch up with today in its step budget refuses the completion, and nothing is written: the date is 1900-01-01, so this holds whatever the date the fixture runs. Both batch writers skip recurrence (`warn_if_batch_skips_recurrence`). Every DONE rides `via: \"command\"`: payload-replayed ops do not run recurrence on the backend. Seed: S1 (Bounded) > S2 (until passed), S3 (until ahead), S4 (count spent), S5 (count 3, seq 1), S6 (seq alone), S7 (until, undated), S8 (count 1, no seq), S9 (`++1d` from 1900), S10 (batch), S11 (property batch). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
